0..68 Comment "// The holders of the roles of inductive-recursive definitions, with"
69..125 Comment "// hypotheses that depart from the canonical hypotheses."
126..128 Comment "//"
129..204 Comment "// The eliminator steps with one proof at each value of the family that the"
205..280 Comment "// arguments hold. Hypotheses of the unit type at every code hold no proof,"
281..337 Comment "// so an eliminator over them would recurse on no field."
338..340 Comment "//"
341..417 Comment "// The checker compares the hypotheses with the canonical hypotheses at each"
418..498 Comment "// constructor of the signature type. The unit type answers at `ι`, and at `σ`"
499..578 Comment "// both sides are the hypotheses at the rest. At `δ` the canonical answer is a"
579..639 Comment "// pair type, so the checker refuses these hypotheses there."
640..642 Comment "//"
643..720 Comment "// - see: `model/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the hypotheses, the map and the"
721..780 Comment "//   eliminator of the family a signature defines, admitted"
781..857 Comment "// - see: `pathological/universe/ir-eliminator.gandr` — an eliminator that"
858..901 Comment "//   calls itself on its own value, refused"
